==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|vegitable||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*weǵ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|vegetable}}, from {{der|en|fro|vegetable}}, from {{der|en|la|vegetābilis|t=able to live and grow}}, derived from {{m|la|vegetāre|t=to enliven}}. Displaced native {{cog|ang|wyrt}} and {{m|ang|ofett#Noun}}.

Related to {{m|en|vigil}}, {{m|en|vigour}}, {{m|en|vajra}}, and {{m|en|waker}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈvɛd͡ʒ.tə.bəl/|[ˈvɛd͡ʒ.tə.bl̩]|/ˈvɛd͡ʒ.ə.tə.bəl/|a=RP,GA}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-vegetable.ogg|Audio (UK)}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-vegetable.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈvɛt͡ʃ.tə.bəl/|a=US,CA}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any [[plant]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1837|title=The Edinburgh New Philosophical Journal|volume=23|page=222
|passage=That he might ascertain whether any of the cloths of ancient Egypt were made of hemp, M. Dutrochet has examined with the microscope the weavable filaments of this last '''vegetable'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Stevenson Treasure Island|text=The first of the tall trees was reached, and by the bearings proved the wrong one. So with the second. The third rose nearly two hundred feet into the air above a clump of underwood — a giant of a '''vegetable''', with a red column as big as a cottage, and a wide shadow around in which a company could have manoeuvred.}}
# A [[plant]] raised for some edible part of it, such as the [[leaf|leaves]], [[roots]], [[fruit]] or [[flower]]s, but excluding any plant considered to be a [[fruit]], [[grain]], [[herb]], or [[spice]] in the [[culinary]] sense.
#: {{syn|en|veg|q1=informal|veggie|q2=informal}}
# The edible part of such a plant.
#: {{syn|en|veg|q1=informal|veggie|q2=informal}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively|derogatory}} A person whose [[brain]] (or, infrequently, whose [[body]]) has been [[damaged]] to the point that they cannot [[interact]] with the [[surrounding]] [[environment]]; a person in a [[persistent vegetative state]].
#: {{syn|en|cabbage}}
# {{lb|en|RAF|slang|historical}} A [[mine]] {{gl|explosive device}}.

